API-18 (distributed CommDelta formula) and PS-API-7 (histogram division): differential test
"same graph, same mapping, sequential view versus distributed view".
dview.c loads a graph as a Dgraph and as a Graph, computes the mapping with SCOTCH_dgraphMapCompute,
saves it, reloads it into the sequential mapping, and prints SCOTCH_graphMapView then "---" then
SCOTCH_dgraphMapView (process 0). dgmap only supports complete-graph targets (kN.tgt).
  sh ../build.sh $WORK/build _pristine
  ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 mpirun --oversubscribe -np 1 ./dview_pristine $V/src/check/data/m4x4_b1_ev.grf $V/tgt/k4.tgt
Pristine (weighted graph): every line identical except
  sequential:  M CommDelta=0.657106   M CommLoad[0]=0.644068 ...   M Processors 4/4 (1)
  distributed: M CommDelta=0.406780   M Cmlosum[0]=0.644068  ...   M Processors 4/4(1)
  (0.406780 = edgeglbnbr / (2 cmlosum) = 48 / 118; 0.657106 = (21 * 24) / (59 * 13))
Patched (commits 0007 + 0008): outputs identical line for line (PartDiam exists only in the
sequential view), for m4x4_b1_ev/k4 (np 1, 2, 3), bump/k9 (np 1, 3), m16x16_b100000/k4 (np 2),
32- and 64-bit. Unweighted graphs already agreed on CommDelta (1.000000) before the fix because
expansion equals dilation when all loads are 1.
PS-API-7: not reproducible: cmlosum == 0 implies every cdsttab cell is 0, hence cdstmax == -1 and
the histogram loop body never runs (same guard structure as the sequential view).
